{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"69c500d422617d2e8d1b16455a1e29907d14f10009a027bf01fb12b52b15d6fd","packTokens":1994,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":252,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":605,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1031,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"A web front end with a small API and a database behind it.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"The app ships with exactly 8 requests.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Requests are stored in the database and survive a reload and a restart.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"The API needs these four operations and no others: list, create, get by ID, and change status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Requests screen with status filters, create dialog, and loading, empty, and error states.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Request detail screen with status-appropriate action, update failure state, and not-found state.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Clean light theme, responsive layout, accessible controls, and specified badge colors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-8\",\n  \"text\": \"Automated tests for the business rules and one end-to-end workflow.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"If the user creates a request while a status filter other than All is selected, how should the list behave after successful creation?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Switch the filter to All so the new Open request appears at the top.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Which browsers must the web app support?\",\n  \"answer\": \"No specific browser support target beyond browsers compatible with the chosen implementation.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"If the create API call fails for a reason other than field validation, what should the dialog show?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Show “Could not create request.” in the dialog, keep the entered values, and allow retry.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"How should surrounding whitespace in a title affect requiredness, length validation, and the stored title?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Trim surrounding whitespace before validating and storing the title.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"After a successful status change on the detail screen, what should happen to the Requests list when the user returns to it?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep the selected filter and refresh the list; the request may disappear if it no longer matches the filter.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Keep 1280 px as the fixed table-layout target.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the 1280 px table-layout target be configurable, or remain the fixed target specified for this release?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Keep the specified detail behavior: show the request on success and “Request not found.” for an unknown ID; add no other fetch states.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the request detail screen add states for loading a request and for failures other than not-found?\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"How should AC-1.1 verify that a newly created request can be retrieved?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Compare the create response with a separate get-by-ID API response.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a browser-accessible maintenance request system with an HTTP API and database that stores requests and preserves them across browser reloads and application restarts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"On empty-database initialization, seed exactly eight requests: four Open, including exactly one Urgent; two In progress; and two Done, with every supported area represented.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Expose exactly four API operations: list requests, create a request, get a request by ID, and change its status; reject attempts to edit fixed fields or delete requests.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Return all requests or those matching one status, ordered newest first; create requests with a system-generated ID, UTC creation time, and Open status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Validate creation fields: a trimmed title of 3–80 characters, a supported area, a supported priority, and an optional description of at most 500 characters; report invalid fields by name.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Allow only Open to In progress, In progress to Done, and Done to Open status changes; reject other changes, return not-found for unknown IDs, and reject missing or unrecognized status-change bodies without changing a request.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Display a Requests screen with the Hive Works wordmark, initials SC, All/Open/In progress/Done filters with All selected initially, a New request button, and a newest-first list.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Refresh the list when a filter is selected or the user returns from detail, retaining the selected filter on return.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Show a new-request dialog with labeled Title, Area, Priority, and Description fields, Normal as the default priority, and Create and Cancel controls.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"On successful creation, close the dialog, select All, and show the new Open request at the top; on field validation errors, keep the dialog open and show the error under the field.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"For non-validation creation failures, show “Could not create request.”, retain entered values, and allow retry.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Show the appropriate loading, empty, or load-error state for the Requests list, with a Retry button for load errors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Show request detail with a back link, title, area, priority and status badges, created date, and description or “No description.” when empty; show the status-appropriate Start work, Mark done, or Reopen action.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"After a successful status change, show the new status and corresponding action; after failure, show “Could not update the request.” and retain the prior status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"For an unknown request ID, show “Request not found.” and a link back to Requests; the API must also identify unknown IDs as not found.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Use a single light theme, sans-serif font, neutral background, near-black text, and labeled status and priority badges with the specified colors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Display dates as date-only values, such as “8 Oct 2026,” without time or timezone; use stacked cards at 375 px and table rows at the fixed 1280 px viewport target, with no horizontal page scrolling at either width.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Label every field, make every control keyboard reachable, and meet WCAG AA text contrast.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Include automated business-rule tests and an end-to-end list-to-completion workflow test, with the specified test cases and successful results.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}